          "guid": "mt2441wzuo26tvox",
          "message": {
            "text": "Preserve selected raster glyphs in the shaped source; suppress only their paint. Skia's macOS scaler sets neverRequestPath for a color typeface but still obtains the same glyph's advance with CTFontGetAdvancesForGlyphs (SkScalerContextmacct.cpp:297-311, pinned revision ebf5052). Replacing the source cluster with U+200B destroyed that advance and shifted all following outlines beneath otherwise-correct overlays. Zero-area structural markers remain the distinct U+200B case; the embedded emitter follows the same metrics/paint split and avoids empty PUA stand-ins.",
            "markdown": "Preserve selected raster glyphs in the shaped source; suppress only their paint. Skia's macOS scaler sets neverRequestPath for a color typeface but still obtains the same glyph's advance with CTFontGetAdvancesForGlyphs (SkScalerContext_mac_ct.cpp:297-311, pinned revision ebf5052). Replacing the source cluster with U+200B destroyed that advance and shifted all following outlines beneath otherwise-correct overlays. Zero-area structural markers remain the distinct U+200B case; the embedded emitter follows the same metrics/paint split and avoids empty PUA stand-ins."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/render/text.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 260,
                  "endLine": 276,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "  // DM-2410: a paint-bearing raster glyph is still part of the shaped source\n  // run. Do not replace it with U+200B before font routing: that destroys the\n  // selected glyph's advance and moves every following outline left. Skia's\n  // macOS scaler makes the same split — a color typeface sets\n  // `neverRequestPath`, but `generateMetrics` still reads the glyph advance\n  // from CoreText (`SkScalerContext_mac_ct.cpp:297-311`, rev ebf5052). Our\n  // path/embedded emitters likewise shape the original source, retain its\n  // advance, and omit only the selected raster representation.\n  //\n  // Zero-area entries are different: they are structural suppression markers\n  // for a separately captured ::first-letter segment and own no paint/advance\n  // in this body run. Those keep the historical U+200B replacement. The raw\n  // `<text>` fallback (`alsoRastered`) cannot inspect selected glyph render\n  // kinds, so it additionally suppresses every overlay that already has paint.\n  const suppress = seg.rasterGlyphs.filter((g) =>\n    (g.suppressGlyph === true && g.rect.width === 0 && g.rect.height === 0)\n      || (alsoRastered && g.dataUri != null));"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
